So the squares language includes all these pairs. It gives you all numbers and their squares with this notation.

706
02:29:29,843 --> 02:29:36,383
Okay, [öğrenci] has a question.

707
02:29:37,483 --> 02:29:43,983
Hocam, what is the difference between alfabet and alfabet with star?

708
02:29:50,388 --> 02:29:52,308
Let's go back to that slide.

709
02:30:01,876 --> 02:30:04,335
Alphabet only has the symbols.

710
02:30:05,056 --> 02:30:05,355
Sorry.

711
02:30:14,611 --> 02:30:31,651
Alphabet only has the symbols, let's say A and B. Alphabet with a star is all the strings that you can obtain using these symbols.

712
02:30:33,907 --> 02:30:39,407
So, A is there, AA is there, AB is there, BA is there, et cetera.

713
02:30:39,407 --> 02:30:49,427
Every string that you can obtain using these symbols are in this set.

714
02:30:50,907 --> 02:30:56,467
And it also includes empty string too.

715
02:31:08,531 --> 02:31:08,971
Okay.

716
02:31:16,691 --> 02:31:34,111
Now, these are sometimes confused. We have an empty language and, sorry. Neye basıyorsan pat oraya atlıyor farede.

717
02:31:51,476 --> 02:31:57,296
So we have two things similar to each other, or you can confuse.

718
02:31:58,296 --> 02:32:04,496
One is empty language, and the other is empty string.

719
02:32:08,835 --> 02:32:12,195
Empty set or empty language is just a set.

720
02:32:18,195 --> 02:32:24,755
Empty string is a string with no symbols.

721
02:32:26,876 --> 02:32:31,095
And you can write a language with empty string.

722
02:32:31,716 --> 02:32:33,716
And it is not empty.

723
02:32:34,135 --> 02:32:35,975
So the language is not empty.

724
02:32:36,475 --> 02:32:38,056
So these are different things.

725
02:32:38,056 --> 02:32:39,995
For example,

726
02:32:45,747 --> 02:32:48,907
Size of empty set is 0.

727
02:32:51,487 --> 02:32:56,627
But size of set with empty string is 1.

728
02:32:58,067 --> 02:33:02,687
Because it has an element in it, even though it is empty.

729
02:33:05,127 --> 02:33:08,407
So you are counting empty string.

730
02:33:16,724 --> 02:33:26,023
So with this empty string and empty set, you need to remember these things.

731
02:33:27,363 --> 02:33:33,844
So for example, a set with an empty string is not empty set.

732
02:33:35,063 --> 02:33:41,523
And set size is for empty strings, empty sets, zero.

733
02:33:44,884 --> 02:33:48,804
When you have empty string there, you add 1.

734
02:33:50,783 --> 02:33:54,923
But the length of empty string itself is 0.

735
02:33:55,923 --> 02:33:58,263
Right? There are no symbols in it.

736
02:34:08,180 --> 02:34:13,700
Now, remember that languages are sets.

737
02:34:14,659 --> 02:34:22,300
That means you have all the usual set operations that you can use with languages.

738
02:34:22,300 --> 02:34:30,620
So you have your union, intersection, difference, complement.

739
02:34:35,316 --> 02:34:41,936
These are all just like sets, set operations.

740
02:34:43,896 --> 02:34:46,495
As languages are sets.

741
02:34:51,347 --> 02:34:56,768
Now, there are some other new operations.

742
02:34:57,148 --> 02:35:01,488
For example, you can define reverse of languages.

743
02:35:04,488 --> 02:35:14,427
Reverse of languages are strings, are the set of strings that are reverse of the original set.

744
02:35:14,427 --> 02:35:18,488
So let's say you have a set AB.

745
02:35:20,211 --> 02:35:27,171
In its reverse, you have ba, right?

746
02:35:27,671 --> 02:35:30,331
The reverse of this string.

747
02:35:30,331 --> 02:35:36,432
So you have the reverse of all strings in the original set, right?

748
02:35:46,804 --> 02:35:51,623
You can also define concatenation of sets or languages.

749
02:35:52,623 --> 02:36:02,263
So this will include all the strings from each set concatenated.

750
02:36:04,263 --> 02:36:11,024
So let's say you have the set A, ABBA as L1.

751
02:36:12,404 --> 02:36:15,463
And L2 is BAA.

752
02:36:16,684 --> 02:36:27,583
Now with A, you need to write all the concatenations in the other set.

753
02:36:27,583 --> 02:36:36,043
So AB, A, AA, right?

754
02:36:38,451 --> 02:36:46,531
Then now in the first set you have AB. With that you write all concatenations.

755
02:36:48,991 --> 02:36:58,051
So you have, so how many elements will this have? This is 3 by 2, 6 elements, right?

756
02:36:58,631 --> 02:37:03,691
It's somehow similar to Cartesian product.

757
02:37:16,468 --> 02:37:18,907
So this was concatenation of languages.

758
02:37:23,407 --> 02:37:26,700
Now, you can define...

759
02:37:29,971 --> 02:37:31,791
The power of a set.

760
02:37:33,752 --> 02:37:42,811
And this is similar to concatenation, but you are concatenating N of the same set, right?

761
02:37:42,811 --> 02:37:51,231
So AB to 3 means you are concatenating 3 of AB.

762
02:37:52,152 --> 02:37:56,051
So you will first concatenate these two.

763
02:37:56,755 --> 02:38:01,195
Then, with that, you will concatenate this last one.

764
02:38:01,916 --> 02:38:06,556
If you want to define based on concatenation.

765
02:38:10,515 --> 02:38:25,995
There is a special case here, by definition, L to the zero is defined as the set with empty string.

766
02:38:27,595 --> 02:38:34,575
So whatever language you have, it's zero power is just this, by definition.

767
02:38:44,435 --> 02:39:10,835
So, let's see. We have this language, A to the end, B to the end. What is its power to? Well, you have one AB, right, from first L, and then you will have another AB set from the second L, but N and M,

768
02:39:12,147 --> 02:39:14,987
don't need to be same.

769
02:39:15,167 --> 02:39:23,567
So you might have ABs with N1 from the first set, 2 from the second set, etc.

770
02:39:23,808 --> 02:39:26,207
So maybe something like this.

771
02:39:27,968 --> 02:39:31,367
AABB can come from first L.

772
02:39:34,268 --> 02:39:37,707
AABBB can come from second L.

773
02:39:46,675 --> 02:39:57,315
Now, one step further, you can define star of these languages.

774
02:39:58,036 --> 02:40:04,995
This is sometimes read as clean star, or we can say this as star closure.

775
02:40:06,995 --> 02:40:09,995
So, star is...

776
02:40:10,388 --> 02:40:18,368
You are unioning, you are taking the union of L to the 0, L to the 1, L to the 3.

777
02:40:19,848 --> 02:40:27,768
So it's a huge, huge set.

778
02:40:29,268 --> 02:40:33,968
And what does it give you?

779
02:40:38,260 --> 02:40:39,860
Concatenations

780
02:40:49,716 --> 02:40:51,416
Of this language.

781
02:40:52,515 --> 02:40:59,136
So, all the concatenations in the strings, of the strings in this language.

782
02:41:00,256 --> 02:41:04,275
So, now string is there again, because we have L0.

783
02:41:06,495 --> 02:41:12,096
Then, L1 is itself, let's say, L itself.

784
02:41:13,175 --> 02:41:14,636
Now, L2.

785
02:41:16,308 --> 02:41:19,228
You are concatenating two L's.

786
02:41:21,108 --> 02:41:30,087
So you can have AA, four B's, A and BB, BB and A.

787
02:41:31,427 --> 02:41:31,708
Right?

788
02:41:32,708 --> 02:41:42,188
Now L3, now you will concatenate L1 and L2.

789
02:41:43,956 --> 02:41:44,476
Right?

790
02:41:45,675 --> 02:41:48,495
And those will be here.

791
02:41:50,576 --> 02:41:55,716
L4 will be concatenation of this guy with L3.

792
02:41:57,175 --> 02:42:08,195
So, at the end, you have all possible concatenations of the strings.

793
02:42:11,347 --> 02:42:15,067
And any number of all possible concatenations.

794
02:42:22,772 --> 02:42:45,512
Now, positive closure is very similar to clean star or what was it? Star closure. So positive closure is similar to star closure. It's just that in the positive closure, you don't have this guy.

795
02:42:49,876 --> 02:42:52,896
You don't have empty string there.

796
02:43:04,628 --> 02:43:11,068
Ok, with this, we finished languages today.

797
02:43:16,211 --> 02:43:35,051
Next lecture, we will see DFAs, deterministic finite automata, and NFAs, non-deterministic finite automata, and we will continue.

